<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        Roles decide what someone can do. A person can hold several. Manage them on
        <a href="/manage/roles">Roles</a>.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="The main roles">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Staff</strong>: the everyday pages, such as My Shifts, My Training and chat.</li>
            <li><strong>Manager</strong>: the Management pages for their location: rota, training, users, compliance
                and so on.</li>
            <li><strong>Admin</strong>: everything, at every location, including Companies &amp; Locations and the
                venue technology (clients, music, projection, automation, DMX). Only an Admin can give or remove the Admin role.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Permission roles">
        <FluentText>These give one extra ability without making someone a manager:</FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>CanPostAnnouncements</strong>: post announcements.</li>
            <li><strong>CanManageFiles</strong>: use the File Manager.</li>
            <li><strong>CanPlayAudioClips</strong>: play audio clips over the venue speakers.</li>
            <li><strong>CanControlMusic</strong>: control the music.</li>
            <li><strong>CanManagePlaylists</strong>: create playlists and add songs to them.</li>
            <li><strong>CanManageDmxSystems</strong>: use the DMX lighting desk.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Giving someone a role">
        <ol>
            <li>Under <strong>User Roles</strong>, use <strong>Select User</strong> to choose the person.</li>
            <li>Their <strong>Assigned Roles</strong> are listed with who added each one and when.</li>
            <li>Use <strong>Assign New Roles</strong> to add one, or the remove button on a role to take it away.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            The <strong>Role Manager</strong> section lists every role. Use <strong>Create a New Role</strong> to add
            one. Disabled roles can be restored, and inactive roles can't be assigned.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
